WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You talk a lot,

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just in the book
but also on your podcast,

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.205 line:92%
about the elections in November.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:08.775
How much confidence do you think
the American people can have

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.477 line:92%
in a fair election right now

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.812
And I do think, you know,
sometimes we talk about it

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a little dangerous,
because obviously

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Trump administration,
based on the outcome,

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
will also speak to the ide
that it was not fair.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, how do you frame it
so that it just doesn't become

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
a thing that everyone
can sort of use

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
for their own best interests
-Yeah.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, everyone is going to
claim that it's rigged.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was the little trick
they pulled in 2016

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
by, you know, Trump constantly
saying it was rigged.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
It forced the Democrats
into this position

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they're like,
"It can't be rigged."

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.740 size:88% position:44%
And then, when it was,
in some respects rigged,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.075 line:92%
they really had nothing to say

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
What they should be doing
is pushing

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
for election transparency
and integrity early.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
They should be pushing
for vote by mail,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:50.817 line:92%
because of the coronavirus

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of the dangers
we are being put in

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.321 line:92%
by having physical voting.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been worried about
the integrity of this election

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a long time,
before the virus came around

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been worried about
domestic voter suppression

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.365 size:78% position:39%
foreign interference,
insecure machines,

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Trump
simply refusing to leave.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:11.871
My new worry is that perhaps
the election will be delayed

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
or kind of
indefinitely postponed.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
Usually, even autocrats
love elections.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they like to hav
a fake election

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that they can brag abou
the people's love.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I didn't think
that Trump would turn down

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.283 line:92%
an opportunity to do that.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
But given this unprecedented
public-health crisis,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's uncertain
what direction he'll go.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.622 line:92%
-Don't take this the wrong way

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:34.394
There is a core pessimism to
a lot of what you write about.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.896
But do you feel as though
there might be a chance

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come through this
on the other side

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:42.135
with a changed perspective
from the American people?

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.871 line:92%
And where do you find optimism

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean,
I don't think about it so much

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms
of optimism or pessimism

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.344 size:88% position:44% line:92%
or hope or hopelessness.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just try to do
the right thing.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, when you have
so much chaos,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you have
so much instability,

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
you really have to look
at your morals

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your principles
and how you treat people

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.823 size:81% position:41%
and the kind of life
that you want to lead.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I just try
to do the right thing.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.961 line:92%
I do try to make suggestions

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are helpful
in that respect.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm not going to have
blind faith

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:16.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
in eroding institutions
that we've already seen fail

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:19.672
You know, what Americans,
I think, have recognized by now,

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
the institutions
are only as good

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the people
who are willing to uphold them

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sometimes they have
to uphold those institutions

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:29.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the face of profound
and unprecedented threats.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so far,
that has not really happened

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.319 line:92%
That doesn't mean it's too late.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't mean
that we're doomed.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
It does mean we're in
for a rough ride

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that we really
have to get our bearings

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:42.996
and focus always on telling th
truth and treating people right.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.999
-Thank you so much, Sarah,
for making time for us again

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, I wish
this would be in the studio.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
And hopefully, next time,
it'll be in person.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:54.541
Please check out Sarah's new
book "Hiding in Plain Sight.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've got a couple of copies
[ Laughs ]

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.245 size:84% position:42%
And we'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thanks, Sarah.

